WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You and Cory Booker -- I know
you have tried to

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:03.570 size:88% position:44% line:92%
spearhead police reform.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is something that
has stalled in the Senate.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you have any optimism
moving forward

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there is
going to be something

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.412 line:92%
that can get through the Senat

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
and make it to
the president's desk?

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:18.785 line:92%
-I'm hopeful, but, you know,

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.153 line:92%
everyone has to participate.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:22.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, the work that
Cory Booker and I did

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
was around the
Justice in Policing Act,

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:28.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
and most of our colleagues o
the Democratic side

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.329 line:92%
in the Senate support it.

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:32.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
On the House side,
there was bipartisan support

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:35.702 size:88% position:44%
for a similar measure,
which has now been named

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:38.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
the George Floyd
Justice in Policing Act.

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:39.105 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And bipartisan support.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:42.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Congressional Black Caucus
was the leader on it.

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:46.546
And I am urging Mitch McConnell,
along with many of us,

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
put it now
on the floor for a vote,

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:51.451 line:92%
because it's just -- It's fair

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.586 line:92%
It's reasonable. It's practical.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
It says that
we should have things like

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.624 size:84% position:42%
a national standard for
excessive use of force.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:00.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
So when a police officer
uses excessive force,

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:03.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
the question we should ask
is not "Was that reasonable?",

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:04.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is what,
currently, we ask.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
We should -- Because you can
reason away anything.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.402 size:78% position:39%
We should be asking,
"Was that necessary?"

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:10.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're saying
that there should be

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
independent investigations
because the prosecutor

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
who works with that
police department every da

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:18.778
will at least have an appearance
of a conflict of interest,

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we want to bring
integrity to the system.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.982
So, these are some of the things
that we're talking about,

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:25.852
and, you know, people are
marching in the streets

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:28.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
by the hundreds of thousands
if not millions.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
People who seemingly have
nothing in common

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:33.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
are joining together
because they are now seeing,

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:38.565
in vivid detail, because o
smartphones, what communitie

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:40.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, in particular, the
black community,

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.234 line:92%
has known for generations.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:44.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there needs to be
accountability and consequence

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:46.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
on this issue,
and we don't need to study it.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've studied it
for generations.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:52.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
Emmett Till's mother was tryin
to help us figure this out

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:55.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
when she had the courage t
leave that open casket

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:59.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
to show the world the brutalit
that we're talking about.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:00.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
We don't need to
study it anymore.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
We need to act, and that's wha
our legislation would do.

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:07.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I encourage everyone to
encourage Mitch McConnell

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
to put it on the floor
for a vote.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:12.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He seems to be
a pretty easily convinced gu

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:15.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
when it comes to bringing
something to vote.

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:17.237 size:84% position:42%
Old Mitch just needs
a little encouragement.

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, yeah,
we can encourage him to pu

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:22.442
the John Lewis Voting Rights Act
on the floor for a vote

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we can put teeth
back into voting rights

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:28.715
and make sure that the elections
that we have coming up

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:31.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
allow everyone to
participate equally.

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:35.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to finish with this.
There is a short list.

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if
you are aware of this.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:37.857 line:92%
There is a short list for V.P.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's, like,
a list of names of people.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
And some would say
that you might be on that list

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:45.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
So do you want to give me
a very safe answer

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:47.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you might have preplanned
that you give to people

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.937
when they say, "Would you
want to be vice president?

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.939 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:57.810
So, okay, let me read my answer.
-There you go.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:58.711 line:92%
We'll just leave it at that.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, but let me --
No, let me say this.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:01.247 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let me say this.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am honored to be
a part of this discussion.

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:09.989
And I say this to you from
the bottom of my heart and soul.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:10.924 line:92%
We have to elect Joe Biden

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:12.091 size:78% position:39%
the next President of
the United States,

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:16.095
and I will do everything in my
power regardless of where I am

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.430 size:78% position:39% line:92%
We have to elect him.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.333
We cannot endure another
four years of Donald Trump

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:23.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
We need a president
who, at this moment in time,

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:27.273
has compassion, who was empathy,
who has a sense of dignity

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:30.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
self-dignity, and lifting up
the dignity of others,

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
somebody who fights
for working families.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:35.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's who Joe Biden is.
I know Joe.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:37.383 line:92%
This is literally who he is.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:40.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we need to save the soul
of our country.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:41.354 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We really do.

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:43.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
We need a president
who cares about

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.226 line:92%
the people and loves the people.

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:48.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
talk about John Lewis.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:48.995 line:92%
Let's connect these two things

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:52.265
You know, part of the leadership
and the power of John Lewis was,

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:54.234 line:92%
he was motivated by love.

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:58.404
-Well, I think that is
a nice place to leave it.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.239 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Thank you so much for

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
making time for us
again, Senator.

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:01.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you, Seth.
Good to be with you again.

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:03.977
-Have a great rest of your week.
-Take care.

